-- title:
--   Corollary 2.3 — tail bound for an independent bounded sum plus conditionally sub-Gaussian later errors
-- statement:
--   There is an absolute constant $c>0$ with the following property. Let $Y_1,\dots,Y_m$ be independent centered random variables with $|Y_i|\le R$ and total variance $V:=\sum_i\mathbb EY_i^2$. Let $D_1,\dots,D_r$ be later errors such that, for every real $\theta$ and every $j$,
--
--   $$
--   \mathbb E\bigl[e^{\theta D_j}\bigm| Y_1,\dots,Y_m,D_1,\dots,D_{j-1}\bigr]\le e^{\theta^2\sigma_j^2/2}\quad\text{almost surely}.
--   $$
--
--   Put $\Sigma^2:=\sum_j\sigma_j^2$. Then for every $t>0$,
--
--   $$
--   \Pr\Bigl[\Bigl|\sum_iY_i+\sum_jD_j\Bigr|\ge t\Bigr]\le2\exp\Bigl(-\frac{ct^2}{V+\Sigma^2+Rt}\Bigr). \tag{8}
--   $$
--
--   When $V+\Sigma^2+Rt=0$ the right side is $0$ (all variables vanish almost surely).
--
--   This is the concentration bound behind the loss and size estimates of Section 6: the initial rounding errors are independent and bounded (Lemma 4.1), and the later rounding errors are conditionally sub-Gaussian (Lemma 4.15).
--
--   **Formalization Note** The conditional expectation is taken with respect to the σ-algebra generated by $Y_1,\dots,Y_m,D_1,\dots,D_{j-1}$; $e^{\theta D_j}$ is assumed integrable, so that the conditional moment generating function is finite.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - reading: for an absolute constant c > 0 → ∃ c > 0 chosen before the probability space and all variables; reason: absolute constant
--   - reading: for every possible history of the earlier randomness → almost surely, conditional on the σ-algebra generated by Y₁, …, Y_m and D_{j'} (j' < j); reason: the standard reading of a conditional expectation bound
--   - encoding: the conditional MGF E[e^{θD_j} | …] → e^{θD_j} integrable for every θ, plus the a.s. bound; reason: the page's bound makes the MGF finite; in Lean a non-integrable conditional expectation is 0, which would make the hypothesis empty
--   - encoding: random variables; |Yᵢ| ≤ R → measurable functions on a probability space; R ≥ 0; reason: a magnitude bound is nonnegative
--   - encoding: the right side of (8) when V + Σ² + Rt = 0 (= 2e^{−∞} = 0) → a separate clause: the probability is 0; reason: Lean's x/0 = 0 would otherwise turn the bound into 2
-- source:
--   Jin–Park–Saha, A Nearly Linear-Time FPRAS for Counting Knapsack, STOC 2027 submission (manuscript sha256 c117260b…), Corollary 2.3, Eq. (8), p.9 (PDF p.10)

import Mathlib

set_option autoImplicit false

namespace KnapsackFPRAS

open MeasureTheory ProbabilityTheory

/-- **Corollary 2.3**, p.9. "Let 𝑌₁, …, 𝑌_𝑚 be independent centered variables with |𝑌𝑖| ≤ 𝑅 and
total variance 𝑉 := ∑ᵢ E𝑌ᵢ². Let 𝐷₁, …, 𝐷_𝑟 be later errors such that, for every real 𝜃, every
𝑗, and every possible history of the earlier randomness,
E[𝑒^{𝜃𝐷_𝑗} | 𝑌₁, …, 𝑌_𝑚, 𝐷₁, …, 𝐷_{𝑗−1}] ≤ 𝑒^{𝜃²𝜎_𝑗²/2}. Put Σ² := ∑_𝑗 𝜎_𝑗². Then, for every
𝑡 > 0, Pr[|∑ᵢ 𝑌ᵢ + ∑_𝑗 𝐷_𝑗| ≥ 𝑡] ≤ 2 exp(−𝑐𝑡²/(𝑉 + Σ² + 𝑅𝑡)) (8) for an absolute constant
𝑐 > 0."

Jin–Park–Saha, *A Nearly Linear-Time FPRAS for Counting Knapsack*, STOC 2027 submission
(manuscript sha256 c117260b…4af0), Corollary 2.3 and Eq. (8), p.9 (PDF p.10).

**Formalization Note.** The constant `c > 0` is chosen before everything else. Random variables
are measurable real functions on a probability space; `R ≥ 0` is the magnitude bound. The
history σ-algebra of `D_j` is the one generated by `Y₁, …, Y_m` and `D_{j'}`, `j' < j`; the
conditional MGF bound holds almost surely, and `e^{θD_j}` is assumed integrable (the page's
inequality presupposes the conditional MGF is finite). When `V + Σ² + Rt = 0` the right side of
(8) is `2e^{−∞} = 0`; this case is stated separately, as the probability being `0`, because
Lean's `x/0 = 0`. -/
theorem corollary_2_3 :
    ∃ c : ℝ, 0 < c ∧
      ∀ {Ω : Type} [MeasurableSpace Ω] (μ : Measure Ω) [IsProbabilityMeasure μ]
        (m r : ℕ) (Y : Fin m → Ω → ℝ) (D : Fin r → Ω → ℝ) (σ : Fin r → ℝ) (R : ℝ),
        0 ≤ R → (∀ i, Measurable (Y i)) → iIndepFun Y μ → (∀ i, μ[Y i] = 0) →
        (∀ i ω, |Y i ω| ≤ R) → (∀ j, Measurable (D j)) →
        (∀ (j : Fin r) (θ : ℝ),
          Integrable (fun ω => Real.exp (θ * D j ω)) μ ∧
          μ[fun ω => Real.exp (θ * D j ω) |
              (⨆ i, MeasurableSpace.comap (Y i) inferInstance) ⊔
                ⨆ (j' : Fin r) (_ : j' < j), MeasurableSpace.comap (D j') inferInstance]
            ≤ᵐ[μ] fun _ => Real.exp (θ ^ 2 * σ j ^ 2 / 2)) →
        let V := ∑ i, ∫ ω, Y i ω ^ 2 ∂μ
        let Sig2 := ∑ j, σ j ^ 2
        ∀ t : ℝ, 0 < t →
          (0 < V + Sig2 + R * t → μ.real {ω | t ≤ |∑ i, Y i ω + ∑ j, D j ω|} ≤
            2 * Real.exp (-(c * t ^ 2) / (V + Sig2 + R * t))) ∧
          (V + Sig2 + R * t = 0 → μ.real {ω | t ≤ |∑ i, Y i ω + ∑ j, D j ω|} = 0) := by sorry

end KnapsackFPRAS
